  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4202.71 Varnish",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4202.71 “Varnish” means a clear or semi-transparent wood coating, excluding lacquers and shellacs, formulated to dry, by chemical reaction, on exposure to air. Varnishes can contain small amounts of pigment to color a surface or to control the final sheen or gloss of the finish.\n\nSource. #8695, eff 7-27-06, ss by #10736, eff 1-1-15 (formerly Env-A 4202.01(bs)); ss by #14202, eff 2-26-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4200.html"
